# ── CordLyx Automated Backups (crontab example) ──
#
# Install: ./backup/setup-cron.sh
# Remove:  ./backup/setup-cron.sh --uninstall
#
# Manual backup: ./backup/backup.sh
#   --db        Database only
#   --uploads   Uploads only
#   --cleanup   Remove backups older than RETENTION_DAYS (default: 14)
#
# Logs: backups/cron.log
#
# The setup-cron.sh script handles path detection and idempotent
# install/uninstall. Use THAT instead of editing this file directly.
